       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A dose of 9,600 mg/day is about three times the maximum ibuprofen dose. At that level the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm is high, and the extra drug adds no benefit. I don't know of any indication where it would be appropriate.\n\nYou have other options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can do that now, for example 800 mg PO three times daily or 600 mg PO four times daily. Both total 2,400 mg/day.\n- **Call pharmacy or a clinical pharmacist.** If you have an unusual reason for this dose, they can review it, document the rationale, and process it through the proper override pathway.\n- **Add other analgesia.** If 2,400 mg/day isn't controlling the pain, acetaminophen or another non-NSAID agent is safer than going above the ibuprofen ceiling.\n\nIf you want one of the first two, tell me and I'll enter it."
